<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Northern Rhodesia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1911">1911</a>–<a href="/years/1964">1964</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Northern Rhodesia was a British territory in south-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, roughly modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a>. Administered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-south-africa-company">British South Africa Company</a> from the 1890s, and as a single territory from 1911, it became a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colonial-office">Colonial Office</a> in 1924. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">Copper</a> mining from the 1920s made it valuable; it belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federation-of-rhodesia-and-nyasaland">Federation of Rhodesia and Nyasaland</a> from 1953 to 1963 and became independent as Zambia on 24 October 1964.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/northern-rhodesia.jpg" alt="Northern Rhodesia" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Greentubing (en:WP talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Northern_Rhodesia_(1939%E2%80%931964).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
